<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 15px;">SPRING SEMESTER: GETTING STARTED!</h3>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h4 style="margin-top: 0;">Registration, step by step!</h4>
      <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>First, speak with a NWC advisor. It's important that you connect with an advisor before you register so you're aware of course details, modes of delivery, and required course supplies.</li>
        <li>To enroll in courses, you may need to take a placement test or provide placement documentation. Students must email to request a placement test: <a href="nwc.advising@alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">nwc.advising@alaska.edu</a>.</li>
        <li>Sign up on your testing placement and potential funding, you will be advised on what courses to enroll into and what course schedule to follow.</li>
        <li>With advisor approval, register for your courses. You may be able to register online through your student account at UAOnline: <a href="https://uaonline.alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">https://uaonline.alaska.edu</a>.</li>
        <li>Verify your enrollment in your secure student account at UAOnline (link above).</li>
        <li>Order your textbooks! See page 4 for details.</li>
        <li>Line up financial aid and funding sources. (See page 6-7 to get started). Scholarships agencies</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <h4 style="margin-top: 0;">How do I browse available courses?</h4>
      <p>This guide is a great place to start! It includes Northwest Campus courses, courses offered by distance from other rural campuses and the Fairbanks campus. To find the most current information across the University of Alaska Fairbanks, visit <a href="https://uaf.edu" style="color: blue;">https://uaf.edu</a>.</p>
      <p>Select "Current Students"</p>
      <p>Select "Class Schedule Search"</p>
      <p>Select "Search by Term"</p>
      <p>Select "Campus" list or "UAF-all campuses"</p>
      <p>Select "Course" and "Subject" (optional)</p>
      <p>Click "Course Search" button at bottom of screen</p>
      <p>Note: The CRNs of the classes you want to take</p>
      <p>If you don't find what you are looking for, contact a NWC advisor for help with your search!</p>
      <p>Email: <a href="nwc.advising@alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">nwc.advising@alaska.edu</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 24px;">REACH YOUR GOALS. THEN, REACH HIGHER</h3>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 30px;">
      <div style="width: 40%;">
        <img src="placeholder.jpg" alt="Michele Adams" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Michele Adams celebrates receiving her certificate in High Latitude Range Management at the 2021 NWC graduation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 60%;">
        <p>Set reachable goals. Once you get there, set new goals! In spring 2021, Northwest Campus student Michele Adams celebrated completing her certificate in High Latitude Range Management. She set a new goal, as she joined the Substitute Teacher Campus Credential program.</p>
        <p>Michele says, "When you earn a degree, you accomplish a big step. You gain knowledge, skills and experience to help you both in your career and in life. In general, on top of that, by gaining additional skills in communication and problem solving and achieving your goals, you can also increase your confidence."</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Visit the UAF Northwest Campus website: <a href="http://www.nwc.uaf.edu" style="color: blue;">www.nwc.uaf.edu</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 24px;">TIME TO ORDER TEXTBOOKS. HERE'S HOW:</h3>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <p>Once you're registered, you need to order textbooks. Students can order books through the UAF Bookstore. You might choose to purchase books through another bookstore, but you first need to visit the UAF Bookstore web site to find out what books you need.</p>
      <p>Note the department, course number, and section number for each of your courses.</p>
      <p><strong>Then:</strong></p>
      <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Go to <a href="https://bkstr.com/alaskafairbanksstore" style="color: blue;">https://bkstr.com/alaskafairbanksstore</a></li>
        <li>Select "Textbooks" near upper left of the screen</li>
        <li>Select your term (semester)</li>
        <li>Enter CRN and click "Shop By Course ID"</li>
        <li>Enter CRN and click "Shop By Course"</li>
        <li>Enter your department</li>
        <li>Enter your course</li>
        <li>Enter your section</li>
        <li>Click "Find Materials for Course"</li>
        <li>View the list of books and materials. You might be able to buy used or new books. It's also possible to rent textbooks.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="margin-top: 0;">Textbook ordering tips and tricks:</h4>
      <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Call for help. Need help ordering books or figuring out how to pay? You can call the UAF Bookstore: 1-888-280-8500 or contact a Northwest Campus advisor for help.</li>
      </ol>
      <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <img src="placeholder.jpg" alt="Bookstore" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 12px;">Get Wrapped Up</p>
        <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 12px;">At the <a href="https://bkstr.com/alaskafairbanksstore" style="color: blue;">https://bkstr.com/alaskafairbanksstore</a> site, click on "Textbooks" to get started.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 24px;">TECHNICAL DIFFICULTIES?</h3>
  <p>Navigating the university websites and online processes can be overwhelming. Have a computer question or problem? Can't see your classes in Blackboard? Forgot your UA email password?</p>
  <p>Contact Gigi Durden, NWC's Technology Specialist:</p>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 20px;">
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <img src="placeholder.jpg" alt="Gigi Durden" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
      <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">Gigi Durden</h4>
      <p>Student Services Technology Specialist</p>
      <p>Based in Nome</p>
      <p>Email: <span data-field="gigi_email">{{ gigi_email }}</span></p>
      <p>Phone: (907) 443-8421 Toll-free: 1-800-478-2202, ext. <span data-field="gigi_ext">{{ gigi_ext }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h4 style="margin-top: 0;">Get Ready for Distance Learning</h4>
      <p>While some courses are offered face-to-face, most courses available to you are taught from a distance. Regardless of the format, make sure you're ready to go for your first day of class!</p>
      <h5 style="margin-top: 20px;">Using ELMO:</h5>
      <p>1. Go to <a href="https://elmo.alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">https://elmo.alaska.edu</a>.</p>
      <p>2. Look up username/ID. Search for my Account.</p>
      <p>3. Enter your birth date, last name, and the last four digits of your social security number, then click "Recover username." (It may take a minute or two depending on your internet connection.)</p>
      <p>4. Answer any security questions to access your account.</p>
      <p>5. Your UA ID Number and UA Username should be viewable. You can change your password in the box on the bottom right side of the screen.</p>
      <h5 style="margin-top: 20px;">Audio Conference (AC):</h5>
      <p>Students participate in class by dialing a toll-free number listed by the course listings starting on page 15. Equipment required: Telephone or headset with microphone, computer with Internet access.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0;">Blackboard (BB):</h4>
    <p>Instruction is delivered online. Equipment required: Computer with Internet access.</p>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">How to log in to Blackboard online:</h4>
    <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Go to <a href="https://www.class.alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">https://www.class.alaska.edu</a>.</li>
      <li>Enter your UA credentials.</li>
      <li>From here, access your courses, grades, and other useful information.</li>
    </ol>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">Blackboard Collaborate (COLL):</h4>
    <p>Accessed through Blackboard online. Equipment required: Computer with Internet access, 256 KB or faster cable or DSL modem, headset with microphone. Depending on your computer's software, downloads may be required.</p>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">Canvas (CVS):</h4>
    <p>Instruction is delivered online. Equipment required: Computer with Internet access.</p>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">How to log in to Canvas online:</h4>
    <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Go to <a href="https://canvas.alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">https://canvas.alaska.edu</a>.</li>
      <li>Enter your UA credentials.</li>
      <li>From here, access your courses, grades, and other useful information.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 15px;">GET YOUR NURSING DEGREE IN NOME</h3>
  <p>Register now for pre-nursing classes!</p>
  <p>The Nome-based associate degree nursing program of the University of Alaska Anchorage will admit its next cohort of four students in January 2023.</p>
  <p><strong>SOUND FAR AWAY?</strong> It's not! You must complete more than 30 credits of pre-nursing courses before applying to the nursing program. If you haven't taken any required pre-nursing courses, consider taking one this semester so you can get started on completing the necessary course requirements.</p>
  <p><strong>START NOW!</strong> Contact a Northwest Campus advisor to register for spring 2022 courses! (See page 2).</p>
  <p style="margin-top: 50px;">Visit the UAF Northwest Campus website: <a href="http://www.nwc.uaf.edu" style="color: blue;">www.nwc.uaf.edu</a></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 24px;">FINANCIAL AID FACTS: SHOW ME THE MONEY!</h3>
  <p>A concern for most college students is how they will pay for classes. Searching for, identifying, and applying for financial aid can be a confusing process. Here is a guide to help you understand all possible scholarships before seeking an educational loan or borrowing money. If you need financial aid applications, help or advising, contact your Northwest Campus advisor (see page 2).</p>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 30px;">Is federal student aid available?</h4>
  <p>The first step in your search for financial aid is completing the Free Application for Federal Student Aid, or FAFSA. Note that timing is key with FAFSA. The federal government opens the FAFSA application for the academic year in which you'll enroll, the more likely it is that funds will be available.</p>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 30px;">Apply online for the FAFSA:</h4>
  <p>Visit <a href="https://www.fafsa.gov" style="color: blue;">https://www.fafsa.gov</a></p>
  <p>UAF's Title IV code (required for the FAFSA): 001063</p>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 30px;">What else do I need to know?</h4>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>It is your responsibility to ensure that all financial aid forms and documents are submitted to the UAF financial aid office by the deadline. If you need help with the financial aid process or have questions about funding options, contact your academic advisor.</li>
    <li>Your classes must be paid by the fee payment deadline of September 3 to avoid paying late fees.</li>
    <li>After all fees, books and tuition have been paid, your remaining funds will be refunded to you via a check in the mail to your mailing address.</li>
    <li>Verify your financial aid status by checking your student account online at <a href="https://uaonline.alaska.edu" style="color: blue;">https://uaonline.alaska.edu</a>.</li>
    <li>Get reminders and additional opportunities through the UAF Northwest Campus and Bering Strait Higher Education Connection Facebook pages. Search #uafnwc and #besc to join!</li>
  </ul>

