<div class="page">
  <div class="header-section">
    <div>
      <h2>STUDENT ACCOUNT RESOURCES</h2>
      <p>Retrieve your UA ID number or username</p>
      <p>Access ELMO—UA's Easy Login Maintenance Option!</p>
      <p>Go to <span data-field="elmo_link">{{ elmo_link }}</span> and follow the directions.</p>
      <p>Having login or technology problems? Contact our Student Services Technology Specialist, Gigi Durden: <span data-field="gigi_phone">{{ gigi_phone }}</span>, ext. 8421, or <span data-field="gigi_email">{{ gigi_email }}</span>.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Update student account information online</div>
      <p>It is your responsibility to keep your mailing and email addresses and phone number updated on UAOnline, so that you receive important communication from Northwest Campus and UAF.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Use your UAF student email account</div>
      <p>Every UAF student is assigned an official UAF email account upon enrollment. The email is only one way some information is distributed from UA. You are responsible for knowing and acting on the contents of all university communications sent to your official UAF email account.</p>
      <p>Make sure you see these emails! Here's how:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Check your UAF email account. Not sure how to access it? Go to <span data-field="ua_email_access_link">{{ ua_email_access_link }}</span>.</li>
        <li>You can forward mail from your UAF account to an email address you check frequently. Learn how here: <span data-field="forwarding_link">{{ forwarding_link }}</span> (click on "How do I forward my email to another account?").</li>
        <li>If for some reason you have multiple UAF email accounts (e.g., a student account and a staff account), forward them to the account you check most often.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="section-title">Attend class</div>
      <p>You might be dropped if you do not attend the first class and have not received prior approval from your instructor. If you do not plan to attend, you must drop your classes by <span data-field="drop_date">{{ drop_date }}</span> to avoid assessment of tuition and fees. The university will drop you from your classes for non-payment.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Check your grades regularly and access your transcripts</div>
      <p>Provided you do not have holds on your account, you can access your official transcript, midterm and final grades at UAOnline.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Log in to <span data-field="uaonline_link">{{ uaonline_link }}</span>.</li>
        <li>Click on the following links:</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="right-column">
      <div class="section-title">Transcripts.</div>
      <p>You may obtain an unofficial transcript online at UAOnline or request one from a member of the NWC student support team (see inside front cover).</p>

      <div class="section-title">Disability Services</div>
      <p>UAF is committed to equal access for students with disabilities. Students experiencing a disability should contact the Disability Services Office at <span data-field="disability_phone_right">{{ disability_phone_right }}</span> or <span data-field="disability_email_right">{{ disability_email_right }}</span>.</p>
      <p>Accommodations are determined through an interactive process that includes a completed application, documentation of the disability and essential requirements of the course.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Information Release & FERPA</div>
      <p>Student records are governed by the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA). For information on the University of Alaska Fairbanks policies, go to <span data-field="ferpa_policy_link">{{ ferpa_policy_link }}</span>. If you have questions about FERPA or wish to request a copied copy of the University's policy, contact the UAF Office of Admissions and the Registrar at <span data-field="registrar_phone">{{ registrar_phone }}</span>.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Student Code of Conduct & Crime Statistics</div>
      <p>UAF students are subject to the UA Student Code of Conduct. For information on this, go to <span data-field="code_of_conduct_link">{{ code_of_conduct_link }}</span>.</p>
      <p>UAF is committed to providing a safe and respectful campus environment free from gender-based violence and sexual harassment. The Title IX Office leads the effort to ensure UAF moves beyond mere compliance and upholds the principles of respect and equality for all.</p>
      <p>For information about the University of Alaska Fairbanks Title IX offices, please visit <span data-field="title_ix_link">{{ title_ix_link }}</span>.</p>
      <p>For information on UAF crime statistics, go to <span data-field="crime_stats_link">{{ crime_stats_link }}</span>. Questions should be directed to the office of Judicial Services on the UAF campus at <span data-field="judicial_services_phone">{{ judicial_services_phone }}</span> (phone), or <span data-field="judicial_services_phone_alt">{{ judicial_services_phone_alt }}</span> (fax).</p>
